// rustc lifetimes/missing-lifetime-in-assoc-type-1.rs — upstream E0207 unconstrained lifetime parameter
// imported batch B167 @ da5114692c9ebe46b869488c5f34f92eb10b98c1 (rust 1.100.0)
// shelf: admit · root lifereg.NEW-E0207
// RE-PORTED AS-IS 2026-09-07 (stage 3). The old port DROPPED THE ASSOCIATED TYPE
// — it kept `impl<'a> ... for &S` but gave the impl no associated type mentioning
// `'a`, so `'a` was merely unused rather than UNCONSTRAINED and E0207 legitimately
// did not fire. It sat in bc_admits_blocked as LEGAL-AS-PORTED. The associated
// type that names `'a` while `'a` appears in neither the trait nor the self type
// is the whole subject of E0207, and it is restored here.
// Original path: tests/ui/lifetimes/missing-lifetime-in-assoc-type-1.rs
// upstream commit: 4b0c9d76ae7d387229caea55cfa73c280b08b8a7
// upstream construct: lines 4-14 —
//     impl<'a> IntoIterator for &S {     //~ ERROR E0207 unconstrained lifetime parameter
//         type Item = &T;                //~ ERROR missing lifetime in associated type
//         type IntoIter = std::collections::btree_map::Values<'a, i32, T>;
// Modifications:
//   · `IntoIterator` -> a local `Tr` with the same two associated types and one
//     method. The stdlib's `IntoIterator<Item>` takes the item as a TYPE PARAMETER,
//     not an associated type, so it cannot carry this test; what E0207 is about is
//     the impl's own lifetime parameter, which is unchanged.
//   · `std::collections::btree_map::Values<'a, i32, T>` -> `&'a i64`. The only thing
//     upstream's `Values` contributes is a SECOND mention of `'a` in an associated
//     type; the concrete container is irrelevant to E0207.
//   · `type Item = &T` (an elided reference upstream reports separately as "missing
//     lifetime in associated type") -> `type Item = &'a T3`, which is the shape that
//     makes `'a` UNCONSTRAINED — the E0207 half, and the half this shelf is about.
//   · the SELF TYPE `&S` is verbatim, with no lifetime written: that is what
//     distinguishes this file from `-5` (`&'_ S`).
//   · struct S/T are unit structs upstream -> one-field structs (`T` is renamed `T3`:
//     `T` alone reads as a type parameter here)
//   · `todo!()` body -> a constant return; assert -> exit code
package missing_lifetime_in_assoc_type_1;
struct S { n: i64 }
struct T3 { n: i64 }
trait Tr { type Item; type IntoIter; fn into_iter(self: Self) -> i64; }
impl<'a> Tr for &S {                // THE DEFECT: admitted, upstream E0207
    type Item = &'a T3;
    type IntoIter = &'a i64;
    fn into_iter(self: Self) -> i64 { return 1i64; }
}
fn main() -> i32 { return 0i32; }
